From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypt32: PFX export and password checks; imported keys get containers of their own

- PFXExportCertStoreEx (and PFXExportCertStore) were stubs. They export
  the store's certificates now, with their RSA private keys when
  EXPORT_PRIVATE_KEYS is given (from the key provider information or the
  key context; REPORT_NO_PRIVATE_KEY and
  REPORT_NOT_ABLE_TO_EXPORT_PRIVATE_KEY refuse what has no key or one that
  cannot be exported), as a PKCS #12 file built with GnuTLS: certificates
  in encrypted bags, keys shrouded (PKCS #12 3DES), local key ids pairing
  them, and a MAC; a NULL pbData asks the size.
- PFXVerifyPassword (a stub, FALSE) says whether the password opens the
  PFX.
- PFXImportCertStore put every imported key in the provider's default
  container, so a second import replaced the first's key; each now gets a
  container of its own named by a GUID. The certificates' key provider
  information said dwKeySpec 3 (the provider's PP_KEYSPEC mask), so
  CryptAcquireCertificatePrivateKey's key spec could sign nothing; it is
  AT_KEYEXCHANGE, the key imported.

Gate: test/pfxexport-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/pfxexport-probe.c: export,
verify, import and sign with the key). Mutant SG_MUTANT_NO_PFX_EXPORT
(crypt32/pfx.c).
---
--- a/dlls/crypt32/crypt32_private.h
+++ b/dlls/crypt32/crypt32_private.h
